Done. Fixed the RFC 2069 digest response computation.

- `httpx/_auth.py:283` — when no `qop` is present, `HA1` was included twice in the digest (`MD5(HA1:HA1:nonce:HA2)`). It now builds `MD5(HA1:nonce:HA2)` per RFC 2069.
- `tests/test_auth.py` — added `test_digest_auth_rfc_2069_response` verifying the exact response hash, and confirmed it fails on the old code and passes now.

All auth tests pass (`86 passed, 1 skipped`); ruff clean. The only mypy error is pre-existing in `httpx/_content.py`.
